              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The clock_gettime() page lists CLOCK_REALTIME, CLOCK_MONOTONIC and the CPU-time clocks; CLOCK_BOOTTIME, CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, *_COARSE and CLOCK_TAI are Linux clocks and are not documented for QNX 8.0."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "QNX 8.0 strategy: Use CLOCK_MONOTONIC for intervals and CLOCK_REALTIME for wall time. If you need time-since-boot semantics, decide what to do while suspended (verify behaviour on your target). timer_create() additionally accepts CLOCK_SOFTTIME. (confidence: verify)",
                "markdown": "**QNX 8.0 strategy:** Use CLOCK_MONOTONIC for intervals and CLOCK_REALTIME for wall time. If you need time-since-boot semantics, decide what to do while suspended (verify behaviour on your target). timer_create() additionally accepts CLOCK_SOFTTIME.\n\n**Why:** The clock_gettime() page lists CLOCK_REALTIME, CLOCK_MONOTONIC and the CPU-time clocks; CLOCK_BOOTTIME, CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, *_COARSE and CLOCK_TAI are Linux clocks and are not documented for QNX 8.0.\n\n- [clock_gettime()](https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/c/clock_gettime.html)\n- [timer_create()](https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/t/timer_create.html)"
