              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "mmap() on QNX documents MAP_ANON (not MAP_ANONYMOUS), MAP_LAZY, MAP_NORESERVE, MAP_STACK and others; MAP_POPULATE, MAP_HUGETLB, MAP_GROWSDOWN, MAP_LOCKED, MAP_32BIT and mremap() are Linux features."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "QNX 8.0 strategy: Use MAP_ANON, drop prefault/huge-page flags (or find the QNX equivalent in the mmap() page), and replace mremap() with mmap + copy. madvise() has no C Library Reference page: use posix_madvise() (documented) (verify). (confidence: verify)",
                "markdown": "**QNX 8.0 strategy:** Use MAP_ANON, drop prefault/huge-page flags (or find the QNX equivalent in the mmap() page), and replace mremap() with mmap + copy. madvise() has no C Library Reference page: use posix_madvise() (documented) (verify).\n\n**Why:** mmap() on QNX documents MAP_ANON (not MAP_ANONYMOUS), MAP_LAZY, MAP_NORESERVE, MAP_STACK and others; MAP_POPULATE, MAP_HUGETLB, MAP_GROWSDOWN, MAP_LOCKED, MAP_32BIT and mremap() are Linux features.\n\n- [mmap()](https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/m/mmap.html)\n- [posix_madvise()](https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/p/posix_madvise.html)"
