            "text": "CPU affinity: cpu_set_t. QNX 8.0: For the calling thread use ThreadCtl(_NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK, &mask) (also _NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK_GET_AND_SET and _NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK_GET_AND_SET_INHERIT); map CPU numbers to bits of the runmask. The ThreadCtl() page says the runmask commands can only be executed on the calling thread, so code that sets the affinity of ANOTHER thread or process (sched_setaffinity(pid, ...)) has no documented equivalent: the target thread must set its own runmask (verify). sched_getcpu() has no documented equivalent: verify. [documented] (already inside a Linux-only #if branch; make sure a QNX branch exists)"
